Subject: stwo-cairo-prover: run the big-stack witness pools inline when threads cannot be spawned

Why (Hellproof S2, wasm64): `partial_ec_mul_window_bits_{9,18}` and `cube_252` build a dedicated
rayon pool with an 8 MiB thread stack (`ThreadPoolBuilder::new().stack_size(..).build().unwrap()`)
around `write_trace_simd`. On wasm without threads `std::thread::spawn` is unsupported, so the
`unwrap` panics (`ThreadPoolBuildError { kind: IOError(Unsupported) }`) — rayon's automatic
single-thread fallback only covers the *global* pool. When the pool cannot be built, run the
closure on the calling thread instead (the wasm shadow stack is sized by the embedder, 16 MiB in
Hellproof). Native behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream: to be submitted as a PR against starkware-libs/proving (base cd7bc5f).

